surfacepro7-camera (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Driver: fail firmware authentication fast behind auth_mutex, so a
    failing setup no longer leaves udev's v4l_id probes stuck at boot.
  * postinst: restart sp7-camerad on upgrade.

 -- Tim Heyne <113726264+Celestial0579@users.noreply.github.com>  @DATE@

surfacepro7-camera (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sp7-camerad: restart a camera session whose libcamera process exceeds
    350 MB (SP7_SESSION_RSS_LIMIT_MB). libcamera 0.7.0's GPU debayer leaks
    one EGLImage per frame (~1.2 MB/min); fixed upstream in 0.7.1.

 -- Tim Heyne <113726264+Celestial0579@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0100

surfacepro7-camera (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package: IPU4P/OV5693/OV8865 drivers (DKMS) with fixes for
    gain step, PCI rename, firmware-auth fail-fast and DKMS module paths;
    IOMMU-identity boot loader; sandboxed on-demand camera daemon with
    suspend handling; udev rules hiding raw ISP nodes; verified firmware
    installer.

 -- Tim Heyne <113726264+Celestial0579@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:15:00 +0100
